Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:36:23 +0800
Subject: dt-bindings: phy: include the clock header the example uses

The clock id split left histb-clock.h as a forwarding shim with
a #warning, and the INNO USB2 PHY example still includes it, so
every dt_binding_check run pays for that warning.

Include the CRG header of the SoC the example describes; the clock id it
takes already lives there under the same HISTB_ name.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)


diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/hisilicon,inno-usb2-phy.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/hisilicon,inno-usb2-phy.yaml
index afd689ec4454..8dc6b67df849 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/hisilicon,inno-usb2-phy.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/hisilicon,inno-usb2-phy.yaml
@@ -70,7 +70,7 @@ additionalProperties: false
 
 examples:
   - |
-    #include <dt-bindings/clock/histb-clock.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-crg.h>
 
     usb2-phy@120 {
         compatible = "hisilicon,hi3798cv200-usb2-phy";
